notes               = "Untitled in source. Written in Isfahan, like moon-lantern and oldest-bridge (pages 96-97). حضیض and اوج are the astronomer's pair — perigee and apogee, the low and high points of an orbit — and also plain words for the worst and best of a life. 3 Dey = 24 December 1990. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

در نگاهم آرام...
در نَفَسم پرموج...
به تو می‌اندیشم...
در هر حضیض... در هر اوج...
اصفهان ۱۳۶۹/۱۰/۳

===machine===

In my gaze, calm...
in my breath, full of waves...
I think of you...
in every trough... at every crest...
Isfahan 1369/10/3

===lantern===

Calm in my looking...
full of waves in my breathing...
I think of you —
at every low point... at every height...

Isfahan 1369/10/3

===translation===

===footnotes===

حضیض and اوج are the technical pair for the nearest and farthest points of an orbit, and
also the ordinary words for the bottom and the top of a life. The English has to choose; it cannot
be an astronomical term and a plain word at once.
